  <!-- Real operational note instead of generic setup tips -->
  <h2>The Refund Policy Is Generous, With One Catch</h2>
  <p>
    AloSIM advertises a no-questions refund if your eSIM won't connect or your device turns out to be incompatible, which is a stronger stance than most eSIM apps take publicly. The catch is timing: that guarantee is for eSIMs that fail to activate, not ones you activated and then didn't end up using much. Buy ahead of a trip if you like (an unused AloSIM plan doesn't expire), but don't activate it until you've actually landed and confirmed you need it, or you lose the refund window along with the data.
  </p>

